## Why This Is Asked
Tests understanding of cross-language callbacks, memory management, and lifecycle handling in CGO bindings, including safety around Go pointers from C.

## Key Concepts
- CGO callback lifecycles and trampolines
- Managing Go function pointers from C via a registry
- Per-subscription context lifetimes and cleanup
- Thread-safety and avoiding GC hazards during C callbacks

## Code Example
```javascript
/* C Header (wrapper.h) */
typedef void (*cb_t)(int, void*);
typedef struct { cb_t cb; void* ctx; } reg_t;
void subscribe(reg_t* r, void* ctx);

/* Go Binding (wrapper.go) */
package main
/*
#include "wrapper.h"
*/
import "C"
import (
  "runtime"
  "sync"
  "unsafe"
)
var reg sync.Map // ctx -> func(int)
//export goEventCb
func goEventCb(event C.int, ctx unsafe.Pointer) {
  if v, ok := reg.Load(ctx); ok {
    if f, ok := v.(func(int)); ok {
      f(int(event))
    }
  }
}
func Subscribe(f func(int)) unsafe.Pointer {
  ctx := C.malloc(C.size_t(8))
  reg.Store(ctx, f)
  C.subscribe((*C.reg_t)(unsafe.Pointer(&C.reg_t{cb: (*C.cb_t)(C.goEventCb), ctx: ctx})), ctx)
  runtime.KeepAlive(f)
  return ctx
}
```

